## Usage Patterns

### Links Only

For links, use `EtFooter.Section` with a row layout style:

```tsx
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  linksRow: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    flexWrap: 'wrap',
    justifyContent: 'center',
    gap: 8,
  },
});

<EtFooter>
  <EtFooter.Section style={styles.linksRow}>
    <EtFooter.Link onPress={handleTerms}>Terms</EtFooter.Link>
    <EtFooter.Link onPress={handlePrivacy}>Privacy</EtFooter.Link>
  </EtFooter.Section>
</EtFooter>;
```

### With Disclaimer and Button

```tsx
<EtFooter>
  <EtFooter.Section>
    <EtText variant="body-tiny-regular">By continuing, you agree to our terms of service.</EtText>
  </EtFooter.Section>
  <EtFooter.Section>
    <EtButton stretch onPress={handleContinue}>
      Continue
    </EtButton>
  </EtFooter.Section>
</EtFooter>
```

### Two Buttons (Main + Subtle)

```tsx
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  buttonsColumn: {
    gap: 12,
  },
});

<EtFooter>
  <EtFooter.Section style={styles.buttonsColumn}>
    <EtButton stretch onPress={handleConfirm}>
      Confirm
    </EtButton>
    <EtButton stretch variant="primary-subtle" onPress={handleCancel}>
      Cancel
    </EtButton>
  </EtFooter.Section>
</EtFooter>;
```

### With Checkbox

```tsx
<EtFooter>
  <EtFooter.Section>
    <EtCheckbox value={checked} onChange={setChecked}>
      <EtCheckbox.Label>I agree to the terms</EtCheckbox.Label>
    </EtCheckbox>
  </EtFooter.Section>
  <EtFooter.Section>
    <EtButton stretch onPress={handleSubmit} disabled={!checked}>
      Submit
    </EtButton>
  </EtFooter.Section>
</EtFooter>
```

### With Horizontal Pagination

Use `direction="horizontal"` for paginated content with dots:

```tsx
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  noPadding: {
    padding: 0,
  },
  footerActions: {
    paddingHorizontal: 36,
    paddingVertical: 24,
  },
});

<EtFooter contentStyle={styles.noPadding}>
  <EtFooter.Scrollable direction="horizontal">
    <EtFooter.Section>
      <EtText>Page 1 content</EtText>
    </EtFooter.Section>
    <EtFooter.Section>
      <EtText>Page 2 content</EtText>
    </EtFooter.Section>
  </EtFooter.Scrollable>
  <EtFooter.Section style={styles.footerActions}>
    <EtButton stretch onPress={handleContinue}>
      Continue
    </EtButton>
  </EtFooter.Section>
</EtFooter>;
```

### With Vertical Scrolling

Use default `direction="vertical"` (or omit) for tall content:

```tsx
<EtFooter>
  <EtFooter.Scrollable>
    <EtFooter.Section>
      <EtText>Long disclaimer text that may need scrolling...</EtText>
    </EtFooter.Section>
  </EtFooter.Scrollable>
  <EtFooter.Section>
    <EtButton stretch onPress={handleAccept}>
      Accept
    </EtButton>
  </EtFooter.Section>
</EtFooter>
```

## Component API

### EtFooter (Root)

| Prop         | Type                 | Description                           |
| ------------ | -------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| children     | ReactNode            | Footer content                        |
| style        | StyleProp<ViewStyle> | Custom container styles               |
| contentStyle | StyleProp<ViewStyle> | Custom styles for the content wrapper |
| testID       | string               | Test identifier                       |
| ...rest      | ViewProps            | Additional View props forwarded       |

### EtFooter.Section

| Prop     | Type                 | Description             |
| -------- | -------------------- | ----------------------- |
| children | ReactNode            | Content elements        |
| style    | StyleProp<ViewStyle> | Custom container styles |
| testID   | string               | Test identifier         |
| ...rest  | ViewProps            | Additional View props   |

**For links layout**, use this style:

```tsx
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  linksRow: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    flexWrap: 'wrap',
    justifyContent: 'center',
    gap: 8,
  },
});

<EtFooter.Section style={styles.linksRow}>...</EtFooter.Section>;
```

### EtFooter.Scrollable

| Prop         | Type                       | Default    | Description                            |
| ------------ | -------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------- |
| children     | ReactNode                  | -          | Content (Sections for horizontal mode) |
| direction    | 'vertical' \| 'horizontal' | 'vertical' | Scroll direction                       |
| style        | StyleProp<ViewStyle>       | -          | Custom container styles                |
| contentStyle | StyleProp<ViewStyle>       | -          | Content styles (vertical mode only)    |
| testID       | string                     | -          | Test identifier                        |
| ...rest      | ViewProps                  | -          | Additional View props                  |

Features:

- **Vertical mode** (default): Simple ScrollView for tall content
- **Horizontal mode**: Paginated scroll with snap-to-page and pagination dots

### EtFooter.Link

| Prop     | Type                 | Description                |
| -------- | -------------------- | -------------------------- |
| children | ReactNode            | Link text                  |
| onPress  | () => void           | Press handler              |
| style    | StyleProp<ViewStyle> | Custom styles              |
| testID   | string               | Test identifier            |
| ...rest  | PressableProps       | Additional Pressable props |

Features:

- Brand-colored text
- Touchable with padding for better hit area
- `accessibilityRole="link"` for accessibility

## Default Styling

- **Container padding**: `paddingHorizontal: X9 (36)`, `paddingVertical: X6 (24)`
- **Section gap**: `X4 (16)` between Section blocks
- **Background**: `colors.backgroundBase` from theme

## Common Tasks

### Adding a New Subcomponent

1. Create the component in `subcomponents/`:

   ```typescript
   export const FooterCustom = memo<FooterCustomProps>(({ children, style, ...rest }) => (
     <View {...rest} style={[styles.container, style]}>{children}</View>
   ));
   FooterCustom.displayName = 'EtFooter.Custom';
   ```

2. Add props interface to `api/types.ts` (extend ViewProps)
3. Export from `subcomponents/index.ts`
4. Add to `EtFooter` compound component in `et-footer.tsx`

### Customizing Content Padding

Override via `contentStyle` prop:

```tsx
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  customPadding: {
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
    paddingVertical: 12,
  },
});

<EtFooter contentStyle={styles.customPadding}>...</EtFooter>;
```

### Removing Default Padding for Horizontal Scrollable Content

When using `Scrollable direction="horizontal"`, remove root padding:

```tsx
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  noPadding: {
    padding: 0,
  },
});

<EtFooter contentStyle={styles.noPadding}>
  <EtFooter.Scrollable direction="horizontal">...</EtFooter.Scrollable>
</EtFooter>;
```

## Best Practices for AI Assistants

1. **Use compound components**: Always use `EtFooter.Section`, `EtFooter.Link`, etc.
2. **For links row layout**: Use `EtFooter.Section` with `styles.linksRow` (define in StyleSheet: `{ flexDirection: 'row', flexWrap: 'wrap', justifyContent: 'center', gap: 8 }`)
3. **Add testIDs**: Include testID on root and key interactive elements
4. **Use EtButton with stretch**: For full-width buttons in footers, use `stretch` prop
5. **Place links at bottom**: Links typically go as the last Section block
6. **Use Scrollable for pagination**: Use `direction="horizontal"` for paginated content with dots
7. **Forward rest props**: All components support additional props via `...rest`
8. **Respect default padding**: Only override when necessary for special layouts

## Troubleshooting

**Q: Pagination dots not showing**
A: Ensure `Scrollable direction="horizontal"` has more than one `Section` child

**Q: Section not full width**
A: Section is centered by default; define `fullWidth: { width: '100%' }` in StyleSheet and apply via `style={styles.fullWidth}`

**Q: Scrollable pages misaligned**
A: Container width is measured on mount; ensure parent has fixed width

**Q: Button not stretching**
A: Add `stretch` prop to `EtButton` for full-width buttons

**Q: Links not horizontal**
A: Define `linksRow: { flexDirection: 'row', flexWrap: 'wrap', justifyContent: 'center', gap: 8 }` in StyleSheet and apply via `style={styles.linksRow}`

